              "annotations": {
                "destructiveHint": false,
                "idempotentHint": true,
                "openWorldHint": false,
                "readOnlyHint": false
              },
              "description": "PROTOTYPE: resolves and builds the current store with the host-granted native XAX compiler ('resolve' then 'build'), writing snapshot/artifact/provenance into the host-granted work directory. Returns the canonical root, artifact byte count and the provenance object (byte count and hex). Artifact handles, entry/package selection, digest reports and toolchain caching are not implemented yet.",
              "inputSchema": {
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {},
                "type": "object"
              },
              "name": "xax_build",
              "title": "XAX build"
            },
            {
              "_meta": {
                "xax-mcp/schema": "xax-mcp-tools-v2"
              },
              "annotations": {
                "destructiveHint": false,
                "openWorldHint": false,
                "readOnlyHint": false
              },
              "description": "PROTOTYPE: resolves and builds the current store, then runs that artifact inside the native OS sandbox and returns exit_code, duration_ms, flags (bit 0 timeout, bit 2 output truncated) and the artifact's stdout/stderr as hex. The sandbox is a capability-less Windows AppContainer inside a job object (fixed limits: 5 s CPU, 256 MiB, one process, 10 s wall, 1 MiB per stream); it ships beside the server as xax-mcp-sandbox.exe and is built from native/xax-mcp-sandbox-gen0.xax. Takes NO arguments yet: the artifact handle, input/output layout, argv, effects and per-call limits fail closed rather than being ignored; Linux namespaces and the xax-mcp-io-v1 framing are not implemented. Requires the host-granted execute right.",
